📑 Project Overview
Purpose: A Java Swing desktop app to manage student records (Name, Course, Section, Credits).
Storage: Uses an ArrayList to save data temporarily in memory.

💻 Code Breakdown (3 Main Parts)
1. Student (Data Model)
Stores student info (name, course, credit, section) using a constructor and Getter methods.
2. StudentOperations (Logic)
ADD: Saves a new student to the ArrayList.
SEARCH: Finds student details using the course name.
UPDATE: Modifies a student's credits and section by matching the course.
DELETE: Removes a record based on the course name.
DISPLAY ALL: Shows all saved records in a clean text format.

3. Studentportal (GUI & Main)
UI Layout: Uses JFrame with absolute layout (null) to position text fields, labels, and buttons.
Events: Implements ActionListener to handle button clicks (Add, Search, Update, Delete, Display).
Error Handling: Uses try-catch to stop crashes if letters are typed into the Credit field instead of numbers.
